  {
    "@id": "https://lighthousetheatre.com/temporary/70e51448-82ec-4e5a-8aa6-1b612425bb87",
    "@type": [
      "http://schema.org/TheaterEvent"
    ],
    "http://schema.org/startDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2023-06-28"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/endDate": [
      {
        "@type": "http://schema.org/Date",
        "@value": "2023-07-15"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/url": [
      {
        "@id": "https://lighthousetheatre.com/event/bed-and-breakfast/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/location": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g1058300"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/image": [
      {
        "@id": "https://lighthousetheatre.com/wp-content/uploads/2022/11/Bed-Breakfast.jpg"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/organizer": [
      {
        "@id": "_:g1058340"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://lighthousetheatre.com/event/bed-and-breakfast/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Bed &#038; Breakfast"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventAttendanceMode": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "http://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<span data-contrast=auto>Brett and Drew want to move out of their tiny downtown condo and into a house, but they just lost their seventh bidding war in Toronto. When Brett’s beloved Aunt Maggie dies, he unexpectedly inherits the historic family home in a quiet little tourist town. Unhappy with their careers and frustrated by life in the fast-paced city, the couple decides to make the move and start up a B &amp; B. But when the guys face friction in their new community, they discover the simple life is more complicated than they thought…</span><span data-ccp-props={&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:160,&quot;335559740&quot;:259}> </span>\n<span data-contrast=auto>With more than a few unexpected and hilarious plot-twists, we follow Brett and Drew over the course of one year— through the real estate rat race, renovation hell, a farcical opening weekend at their B &amp; B, and encounters with small-town prejudice—all the way to their big decision: do they stay here or do they pack it all in?</span><span data-ccp-props={&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:160,&quot;335559740&quot;:259}> </span>\n<span data-contrast=auto>With dozens of characters—male and female, young and old—all portrayed by two men, Bed and Breakfast is a theatrical tour de force. As riotously funny as it is deeply moving, this is a heartfelt comedy about being out in small town Canada, skeletons in the closet, and finding a place to call home.</span><span data-ccp-props={&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559739&quot;:160,&quot;335559740&quot;:259}> </span>\n<em><strong><span class=ui-provider deh dei c d e f g h i j k l m n o p q r s t dej dek w x y z ab ac ae af ag ah ai aj ak dir=ltr>This play includes strong language which may be offensive to some viewers.</span></strong></em>\n"
      }
    ]
  },
