    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A Tragically Hip Matinee Show Featuring 50 Mission"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventAttendanceMode": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "http://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "&#8220;Canada’s Sound. Gord’s Spirit. One Unforgettable Afternoon.&#8221;\nThe Tragically Hip is a band that defined a generation. It’s about more than music—it’s about memory, identity, and national pride. For <span class=outlook-search-highlight data-markjs=true>50</span> <span class=outlook-search-highlight data-markjs=true>Mission</span>, every note is a tribute to the poetry, passion, and poignancy that made The Hip a household name from coast to coast to coast.\nThis show is a chance to relive the soundtrack of Canada’s collective experience. Whether you grew up with Ahead by a Century, sang &#8220;Wheatkings&#8221; around the cottage campfire or found solace in Grace, Too, <span class=outlook-search-highlight data-markjs=true>50</span> <span class=outlook-search-highlight data-markjs=true>Mission</span> invites you to sing, sway, and celebrate the band that made us feel truly Canadian.\n<span class=outlook-search-highlight data-markjs=true>50</span> <span class=outlook-search-highlight data-markjs=true>Mission</span> isn’t just a tribute—it’s a heartfelt homage to the soul of Canadian rock. Named after the legendary Hip song <span class=outlook-search-highlight data-markjs=true>50</span><span class=outlook-search-highlight data-markjs=true>Mission</span> Cap, this band channels the raw energy, poetic lyricism, and unmistakable sound of The Tragically Hip with reverence and authenticity.\nFrom the haunting storytelling of Wheat Kings to the stadium-shaking power of Blow at High Dough, <span class=outlook-search-highlight data-markjs=true>50</span> <span class=outlook-search-highlight data-markjs=true>Mission</span> delivers a full-spectrum experience that satisfies both casual listeners and die-hard fans. Every performance is a celebration of Gord Downie’s legacy and the band’s enduring impact on Canadian culture.\n"
      }
    ]
  },
