      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "UK Calling"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventAttendanceMode": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "http://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "UK Calling are coming to Port Dover!!\nNot just some 80s show, UK Calling pay tribute to an era, a vibe and a style. Just like Toronto’s old CFNY-FM, this show brings alternative hits from the late 70’s and 80’s, focusing on artists like The Clash, Tears for Fears, The Cure and The Specials, the repertoire covers the best from New Wave, Post-Punk and 2tone Ska from the era.\nWhat separates this show from the rest is the energy brought to the performance. More than a pair of wayfarers and a cheesy synthesizer, this band digs in and works their hearts out to bring audiences a dynamic and animated show that keeps people dancing all night. UK Calling play the songs that nobody else does. Style Council, Joy Division, Madness – if you know who these are, you will love UK Calling. For those that are new to the genre, the engaging performance and the world-class tenor voice of entrancing frontman Peter James Fox, will pull you in and take you on a journey that will leave you saying ‘Wow!’\nFresh from sold out shows across Ontario, UK Calling will be bringing their evening of classic New Wave, 2 Tone Ska, and Post-Punk vibes of the late 70s and early 80s to the Lighthouse Theatre on November 21. This is your exclusive invitation to an evening where nostalgia isn&#8217;t just welcomed; it&#8217;s celebrated. UK Calling always make it a night to remember, so get out your black eye-liner, dust off your docs and get ready to dance all night!\nSince 2018, UK Calling has been the name on everyone&#8217;s lips, turning ordinary nights into extraordinary memories. So, why settle for the usual when you can be part of something truly special?\n"
      }
    ]
  },
