    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "NIGHT FEVER\nTHE BEE GEES SHOW\nNight Fever is the world’s number one production of the Bee Gees. This all Canadian cast from Toronto, Ontario, will take you back in time to one of the greatest bands in pop history.\nFrom the early years to the disco era, you will hear all the hits from Too Love Somebody, How Can You Men a Broken Heart, More Than a Woman, Jive Talking, How Deep Is Your Love to You Should Be Dancing.\nThe Bee Gees span over 50 years of hit songs and have been inducted into the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame.\nNight Fever features the vocals and look of the Bee Gees with Carm Castiglione as Barry Gibb, Joe Varga as Robin Gibb and Daryl Thistle as Maurice Gibb.\nThe songs are done note for note, chord for chord, exactly like the record.\nBacked by a live band of studio musicians, the sound is so close that you will think you are hearing the original recording.\nSit back and enjoy the greatest tribute ever to the Bee Gees from Canada, NIGHT FEVER!\nLA TIMES- An incredible tribute to the Bee Gees\nGLOBE&amp;MAIL – Night Fever, is a fantastic show\n"
      }
    ]
  },
