    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<strong>Fireside Munsch Classics</strong> is a laugh-out-loud, high-energy celebration of some of Canada’s most beloved children’s stories. Starring the wildly entertaining M. John Kennedy, this playful production brings four classic Robert Munsch tales to life in one wacky, fast-paced storytelling adventure. Audiences will delight in the outrageous antics of <strong>50 Below Zero</strong>, the silliness of <strong>PIGS</strong>, the heartwarming surprises of <strong>Something Good</strong>, and the unforgettable heroine of <strong>The Paper Bag Princess</strong>.\nPerformed as a single, whirlwind play, Fireside Munsch Classics captures the joy, imagination, and mischievous spirit that have made Robert Munsch a household name for generations. With big characters, physical comedy, and plenty of audience engagement, this show keeps kids giggling and grown-ups smiling from start to finish.\nPerfect for families, school-aged children, and anyone who grew up loving Munsch stories, this energetic theatrical experience proves that great storytelling never goes out of style.\n| Suitable for All Ages |\n"
      }
    ]
  },
