    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "<em>Curtains</em><span data-contrast=auto> is a side-splitting Broadway musical comedy where murder meets musical theatre &#8211; and the result is pure showbiz gold. Set in 1959 Boston, the story begins on the opening night of a brand-new (and not-so-brilliant) musical called </span><i><span data-contrast=auto>Robbin’ Hood</span></i><span data-contrast=auto>. When the show’s talentless leading lady drops dead mid-bow, it’s up to the charmingly awkward Detective Frank Cioffi, a cop with Broadway dreams of his own, to solve the case before the killer strikes again.</span><span data-ccp-props={&quot;134233117&quot;:true,&quot;134233118&quot;:true,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}> </span>\n<span data-contrast=auto>As the cast and crew scramble to save both the show </span><i><span data-contrast=auto>and</span></i><span data-contrast=auto> their necks, what unfolds is a hilariously campy mash-up of mystery, romance, and razzle-dazzle. Packed with catchy Kander and Ebb tunes, witty wordplay, and a script that pokes loving fun at the world of theatre itself, </span><i><span data-contrast=auto>Curtains</span></i><span data-contrast=auto> proves that sometimes the only thing more dramatic than a murder is an opening night.</span><span data-ccp-props={&quot;134233117&quot;:true,&quot;134233118&quot;:true,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}> </span>\n<span data-contrast=auto>Filled with backstage gossip, dance numbers, and enough jazz hands to cover a crime scene, </span><i><span data-contrast=auto>Curtains</span></i><span data-contrast=auto> is a laugh-out-loud love letter to anyone who’s ever missed their cue, flubbed a line, or dreamed of hearing applause. It’s a musical comedy with a </span><i><span data-contrast=auto>killer</span></i><span data-contrast=auto> twist &#8211; literally!</span><span data-ccp-props={&quot;134233117&quot;:true,&quot;134233118&quot;:true,&quot;201341983&quot;:0,&quot;335559740&quot;:240}> </span>\n<strong>Content Advisory</strong>\n<em>Please note that Curtains contains mature themes and some coarse language. While presented as a comedic musical, this production may not be suitable for all audiences. Patrons are encouraged to use their best judgment when considering this performance for younger children.</em>\n"
      }
    ]
  },
