    "http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#wasDerivedFrom": [
      {
        "@id": "https://lighthousetheatre.com/event/the-linda-ronstadt-show/"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Linda Ronstadt Show"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventAttendanceMode": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "http://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Experience the magic of Linda Ronstadt like never before. This powerful Docu-Concert brings to life the music and story of one of the most versatile and influential vocalists of the 20th century.  From heart-wrenching ballads to country-rock anthems, this acclaimed live tribute captures the essence of Ronstadt’s remarkable life and career with a dynamic performance that resonates with fans old and new.\nThe Linda Ronstadt Show is not like any other tribute!  This show is like a rock concert and a musical rolled into one—combining the power of live music, heartfelt storytelling, and rare video footage. Audiences not only hear Linda’s unforgettable songs, they also experience the incredible journey behind them.\nLinda Ronstadt was more than a superstar—she was a musical force who defined an era. She helped launch the careers of The Eagles and collaborated with legendary artists, including Dolly Parton, Emmylou Harris, Aaron Neville, James Taylor, and Neil Young.\nStarring powerhouse vocalist Karen Coughlin, backed by a band of top-tier Canadian musicians, this show delivers a stunning note-for-note tribute to one of the most iconic and groundbreaking artists of all time. Whether you&#8217;re a lifelong fan or discovering her music for the first time, this is a must-see celebration of one of the greatest voices in popular music.\nA portion of proceeds supports Parkinson Canada, helping fund research, support services, and advocacy for Canadians living with Parkinson’s.\nGet your tickets now before they sell out!\n"
      }
    ]
  },
