    "http://schema.org/name": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Tapestry, the Carole King Songbook"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventAttendanceMode": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "http://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/eventStatus": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "http://schema.org/EventScheduled"
      }
    ],
    "http://schema.org/description": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Tapestry, the Carole King Songbook – Starring Suzanne O Davis.\nNorth America’s Premier Tribute to Carole King\nThis show recreates the sound and vibe of a 1970’s Carole King concert experience following her legendary album, &#8216;Tapestry&#8217;. You will love hearing the timeless music behind the iconic image of her 1971 multiple Grammy-winning album. Suzanne delivers a ‘docu-concert’ style presentation that includes entertaining stories, funny anecdotes, lots of audience participation, and multimedia that enhances this celebrated music.\nSuzanne O Davis and her world-class band perform the complete ‘Tapestry’ album. They also bring to life many hits featured in the Broadway smash, ‘Beautiful’, including songs that Carole and her husband, Gerry Goffin, wrote in the 1960s. Together, they composed more than 400 songs recorded by artists such as The Drifters, The Beatles, Herman’s Hermits, Donnie Osmond, Aretha Franklin, The Shirelles, Bobby Vee, and the list goes on&#8230;\nTapestry delivers more than just an exceptional concert &#8211; it’s a joyful celebration of the songs that reshaped the pop music landscape.\nYou will feel the Earth move under your feet with this show!\n"
      }
    ]
  },
