      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Welcome to Il Glorioso Buco, Toronto&#8217;s swankiest, most suspiciously well-staffed Italian restaurant. It&#8217;s opening night, the risotto is simmering, and the atmosphere is thick with… espionage? That&#8217;s right &#8211; unbeknownst to the hungry guests and hapless staff, a crack team of international spies has taken over the kitchen, using marinara as camouflage for a top-secret sting operation. Enter Harry Marsden: an eternally optimistic rookie who thinks he&#8217;s just starting a regular old waiter gig. Dressed to impress in his ill-fitting tux and armed only with a serving tray and way too much enthusiasm, Harry has no idea he&#8217;s just walked into the culinary equivalent of a James Bond blooper reel. Featuring tuxedoed takedowns, linguini larceny, suspicious accents and one very confused maître d&#8217;, this world premiere is Mission: Impossible meets slapstick as Secret Service proves the biggest secret might just be Harry&#8217;s complete cluelessness. Spies, lies, and al dente drama &#8211; what could possibly go wrong?\n"
      }
    ]
  },
