        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Four long-time friends pile into a well-worn car and set off on the ultimate cross-country road trip: from Toronto all the way to Dildo, Newfoundland. What starts as a spontaneous getaway soon spirals into a journey full of chaos, confession, and more than a few questionable roadside snacks. Armed with nothing but a scrapbook, a cooler full of kombucha, and decades of shared history, the women relive old memories, create outrageous new ones, and take on everything from skinny dipping in questionable lakes to navigating tourist traps with names they definitely can&#8217;t say on the radio. Secrets are spilled, boundaries are tested, and laughter erupts at every turn. As the kilometres roll by, the miles on their friendship deepen. The Beaver Club is a raucous, unfiltered, and surprisingly touching celebration of womanhood, aging disgracefully, and friendships that can survive anything.\n"
